            'indian_applicant_html' => '<h4 style=\'margin:0 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>A Genuine, Officially Named Medical Visa</h4><p>Colombia\'s Visa V for medical treatment is confirmed directly on the Cancilleria\'s official website, requiring a physician\'s certificate, proof of financial solvency, and the signed DP-FO-67 form.</p><h4 style=\'margin:20px 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>A Companion Can Be Included, But Must Still Qualify</h4><p>Colombia is unusual in formally allowing a companion to be added as a documented beneficiary of the same visa application, provided economic dependence and a notarised responsibility letter are shown — this is not automatic coverage, and the companion\'s eligibility is assessed on its own terms.</p><p>Our consultants can help assemble the physician certificate, financial solvency proof, and companion documentation this visa requires.</p>',
