            'indian_applicant_html' => '<h4 style=\'margin:0 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>No Short-Term Medical Visa</h4><p>For a short treatment visit, Costa Rica is reported to rely on its ordinary tourist-entry route rather than a dedicated medical visa — though whether that route is visa-free or requires an advance consular visa for Indian citizens is itself disputed between sources, so this should be confirmed with the Costa Rican embassy before booking.</p><h4 style=\'margin:20px 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>A Distinct Long-Stay Route for Extended, Hospital-Sponsored Treatment</h4><p>For extended treatment, a reported "Estancia" (non-resident stay) category under Article 150, for a person requiring specialised treatment at a recognised hospital, is genuinely distinct from the Residencia Temporal framework used for other purposes — it is a separate legal basis, not a variant of Residencia Temporal.</p><p>Our consultants can help clarify, with the Costa Rican embassy and DGME, which of these two routes fits a specific treatment plan.</p>',
